            },
            required: ["generated_doc_content", "generation_status"]
        }
    },

    prompt_source: {
        type: "inline",
        content: """
        You are tasked with generating a comprehensive documentation file (e.g., a README.md in Markdown format) for a newly created rule and its ecosystem.

        Rule ID: {{rule_creation_context.rule_id}}

        Core Rule File Information:
        Path: {{rule_creation_context.core_rule_file_info.file_path}}
        Description: {{rule_creation_context.core_rule_file_info.rule_description}}
        Input Schema Summary: {{rule_creation_context.core_rule_file_info.input_schema_summary}}
        Output Schema Summary: {{rule_creation_context.core_rule_file_info.output_schema_summary}}
        (Additional core rule details as available...)

        Associated Knowledge Base (KB) Artifacts:
        {{#each rule_creation_context.created_kb_artifacts}}
        - KB Artifact:
          Path: {{this.file_path}}
          Type: {{this.artifact_type}}
          Purpose: {{this.kb_purpose}}
          Summary: {{this.content_summary}}
        {{/each}}

        Documentation Requirements (from manifest):
        Expected Sections: {{#join rule_creation_context.target_documentation_manifest_entry.main_sections_to_include ", "}}{{/join}}
        Target Path (for reference): {{rule_creation_context.target_documentation_manifest_entry.target_path}}

        Please generate the documentation content. It should typically include:
        1.  An overview of the rule: What it does, its purpose.
        2.  How to use the rule: Inputs, outputs, expected behavior.
        3.  Dependencies: Any other rules or KBs it directly relies on (beyond those listed as part of its own ecosystem).
        4.  Associated KBs: A list or description of the KBs created alongside this rule (examples, prompts, specs), explaining their role.
        5.  Key sections as specified in the manifest.
        6.  (Optional) Auto-documentation of input/output schemas if complex.
        
        Format the output in clear, well-structured Markdown. 
        Your entire response will be treated as the documentation file content.
        """
        // Note: Actual implementation would require more detailed placeholders in the prompt
